                <pb facs="0778" n="628" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg628"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 3691/383.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of Salvador
                        to President Roosevelt.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador, Salvador</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1907-04-08"><hi rendition="#italic">April 8,
                                1907</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Very sincere thanks for considerate complaisance respecting continuation peace
                    negotiations by Chargé Brown. Whatever good result is achieved will be due to
                    the good offices of your Government and you will have the thanks of Central
                    America.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Figueroa.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
